# Local-only audit report (senior read-only review). Never committed.
/AUDIT.md

# Obsidian vault that happens to live in the working copy. Not part of the
# product, and untracked-but-unignored meant a stray `git add -A` would commit it.
/io/

# Local agent wiring, written into whatever repo the sidecar governs.
# Machine-specific (absolute binary paths, ports, a mined policy) and never the
# same on two checkouts. Same class as .claude/ above.
.iaga/
.codex/
.cursor/

# The coding-agent skill is a self-contained Node package on its way to its own
# repository: it is NOT a Cargo workspace member and is not released with the
# sidecar. Keeping it untracked-but-unignored meant a stray `git add -A` would
# commit half a second product.
sentinel-skill/

# Internal working prompts for release/audit sessions. Italian, process-
# specific, and about how the work was driven rather than how the product works;
# the public docs are English. Same posture as /AUDIT.md.
docs/demo/PROMPT_*.md
/.audit/
